.TH CHRONICLE 1 "2026-07-24" "chronicle 1.0" "InterGenOS System Administration"
.SH NAME
chronicle \- back up and restore system and user data over time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chronicle
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.I command
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chronicle
is the command-line client for the InterGenOS backup engine
.BR chronicled (8).
It keeps a browse-by-time history of three layers:
.TP
.B config state
every version of the system's configuration (\fI/etc\fR and package state),
kept in an always-on content-addressed store on the system disk so the machine
has some protection before any external drive is attached.
.TP
.B user data
the bulk home-directory history, captured hourly to the external target by
hardlink rotation while the target is present.
.TP
.B restore points
a snapshot of exactly a package transaction's footprint plus the package
database, taken before every
.BR pkm (1)
install, upgrade, or remove.
.PP
An external target is labelled honestly: a POSIX volume is
.BR ready ,
a FAT/exFAT volume is shown as
.B must reformat
(the hardlink/ownership model requires a POSIX filesystem), and a volume on the
same physical disk as the system is disqualified.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show target health and per-layer capture recency.
.TP
.BR list " \fILAYER\fR [\fB\-\-since\fR \fIEPOCH\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR \fIEPOCH\fR]"
Browse a layer's timeline. \fILAYER\fR is
.IR config-state ", " user-data ", or " restore-point .
.TP
.BR capture " \fILAYER\fR [\fIPATH...\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-async\fR]"
Take a version now. \fB\-\-async\fR enqueues the capture for the off-peak window
instead of running it immediately. \fB\-\-reason\fR text is stored with the
version and is shown by
.B list
to every caller permitted to read backup status, which is any account in the
.B chronicle
group \(em not only administrators. Reasons generated by
.BR pkm (1)
name packages; a reason typed here should be treated the same way.
.TP
.BR diff " \fILAYER\fR \fIVERSION\fR \fIPATH\fR"
Show a then-vs-now diff for a path against a stored version.
.TP
.BR restore " \fILAYER\fR \fIVERSION\fR \fIPATH...\fR \
[\fB\-\-mode\fR replace-confirm|beside] [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR]"
Restore paths from a version. A restore is
.B never
silent: the plan is shown and confirmed first (\fB\-y\fR skips the prompt,
\fB\-\-dry-run\fR shows the plan only). \fB\-\-mode beside\fR writes each file
next to its original instead of overwriting; a config-layer restore lands as a
.I .pkmnew
reviewed change rather than a silent revert. Every file is re-hashed before it
is written. A restore that must recreate ownership is carried out by the
higher-capability
.BR chronicle-restore@ (8)
leg.
.TP
.BR verify " [\fILAYER\fR] [\fIVERSION\fR] [\fB\-\-scrub\fR]"
Verify a version's integrity, or with \fB\-\-scrub\fR re-hash the whole store
and name any corrupt blob together with every version that references it.
.TP
.BR target " scan"
Enumerate candidate target volumes with their labels.
.TP
.BR target " adopt \fIMOUNTPOINT\fR [\fB\-\-class\fR whole-volume|directory] \
[\fB\-\-device\fR \fIDEV\fR] [\fB\-\-cap\fR \fIBYTES\fR]"
Initialize a target. The
.B directory
class owns only \fIMOUNTPOINT\fR/ChronicleBackups up to \fB\-\-cap\fR bytes and
never touches the rest of the volume.
.TP
.BR pin " \fIVERSION\fR"
Protect a version from all pruning, including volume-full pruning.
.TP
.BR unpin " \fIVERSION\fR"
Release a pin.
.TP
.B queue
Show the deferred-capture queue ("N changes queued \(em will back up after
<working-hours>").
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show more detail.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Errors only.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON output.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the restore confirmation prompt.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/chronicle/
The always-on local store (config-state + restore points, engine state).
.TP
.I /etc/chronicle/chronicle.conf
Configuration \(em see
.BR chronicle.conf (5).
.TP
.I /run/chronicle/engine.sock
The engine IPC socket, owned
.BR root:chronicle ", mode " 0660 .
An account outside the
.B chronicle
group cannot open it, and
.B chronicle
reports that rather than reporting the engine as stopped. An administrator
grants it with
.BR "usermod \-aG chronicle \fIUSER\fR" ;
the account picks it up at its next login.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Restore a file to how it was at a point in time (preview first):
.PP
.RS
.nf
chronicle restore user-data v42 /home/ada/notes.md \-\-dry-run
chronicle restore user-data v42 /home/ada/notes.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pin a version so it is never pruned:
.PP
.RS
.nf
chronicle pin v42
.fi
.RE
.PP
Scan for and adopt a backup target:
.PP
.RS
.nf
chronicle target scan
chronicle target adopt /run/media/ada/backup
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chronicled (8),
.BR chronicle.conf (5),
.BR pkm (1),
.BR forge (1)
